From: mbox
Subject: drm: give devtmpfs-created render nodes mode 0666

The mbox guest mounts devtmpfs directly and runs no udev, so device
nodes keep the kernel defaults.  drm_sysfs.c's devnode callback only
supplies the path ("dri/%s"), leaving the default 0600/root for card0
and renderD128.  Real distributions get 0666 render nodes via udev
rules; a headless guest without udev gets neither.

Unprivileged guest sessions (the engine maps the host uid) therefore
could not open /dev/dri/renderD128, and the venus Vulkan driver saw no
render device.  Give DRM_MINOR_RENDER nodes 0666 in the devnode
callback, which devtmpfs honours at node creation time.  card0 stays
0600 (it is a KMS node; the GPU compute path only needs the render
node).
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_sysfs.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_sysfs.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_sysfs.c
@@ -96,4 +96,8 @@ static char *drm_devnode(const struct device *dev, umode_t *mode)
 static char *drm_devnode(const struct device *dev, umode_t *mode)
 {
+	struct drm_minor *minor = to_drm_minor(dev);
+
+	if (mode && minor->type == DRM_MINOR_RENDER)
+		*mode = 0666;
 	return kasprintf(GFP_KERNEL, "dri/%s", dev_name(dev));
 }
